Move morphism kinds and surjectivity to algebra/

MorphismKind { If, SurjThen, NonSurjThen, Noop } and morphism_kinds on
RuleStructures, populated as walk_stmt clones each statement's
after-structure. The kind is metadata about the AST construct that
produced the morphism, not an algebraic property of the morphism itself.

Port the el_should_be_surjective_ok / el_is_surjective_ok check from
eqlog.eql to a Rust-side scan in algebra/build_structures: every element
of a then-atom morphism's target must be in the morphism's image, with
the defined-then atom's term el exempt for NonSurjThen. Drop the
now-redundant eqlog.eql rules and the iter_surjectivity_errors consumer.
